---
title: Pumpkin olive oil loaf
servings: 9
yield: two 9x5-inch loaves
tags: [fall, thanksgiving]
source: Pumpkin Olive Oil Loaf by Ovenly, https://www.oven.ly/recipes/project-four-yjynj-cs8g8-lnk4f
---

Heat the oven to 350°F. Butter two #9x5-inch loaf pans{} with @unsalted butter{}(softened) and dust them with @all-purpose flour{}.

Whisk the @all-purpose flour{3 1/2%cup}, @baking soda{2%tsp}, @salt{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground cloves{1%tsp} and @ground ginger{1%tsp} together in a #medium bowl{}.

Melt the @unsalted butter{1/2%cup} in a #small saucepan{} over low heat and let it cool.

In a #stand mixer{} with the paddle, beat the @granulated sugar{3%cup}, @pumpkin puree{2%cup}, @water{2/3%cup}, @olive oil{1/2%cup} and the melted butter until smooth.

On medium-low, add the @eggs{4}(room temperature) one at a time, mixing each in.

Add the dry mix in three goes on low speed. After the last, mix ~{15%seconds} more so no flour is left at the bottom.

Divide the batter between the pans and scatter @pepitas{}(raw) and @turbinado sugar{} over the top.

Bake ~{60%minutes} to 65 minutes, until a skewer in the middle comes out clean.
